# Backend

Model the domain in explicit types and functions. Keep request handling, domain rules, and persistence adapters separate.

Define failure behavior: what retries, what is idempotent, what aborts, and what the caller observes. Timeouts are part of the interface.

Protect invariants in one place, not in every caller. Multi-step writes state their consistency expectation.

Background work is visible: status, retry, and a way to detect a stuck job. Do not add a queue until synchronous handling fails a real constraint.

Logs and errors must be diagnosable without secrets or unnecessary raw user content.
